    rel:notation "x·inv(x) = e" ;
    rel:left   term:inverse:left ;
    rel:right  term:inverse:e ;
    rel:member case:inverse:zero ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The LEFT inverse law x·inv(x) = e — side 1 of the abelian-group two-sided inverse, INHERITED from group and restated at family:abelian:group, reified as an equation record (rec:equation:record) with one @rel:left term (x·inv(x)) and one @rel:right term (e). A two-sided law mints TWO equation records, one per side (design §1.6, §3; closure.ttl:185-192 case:zero/case:one precedent). [S] the species:inverse:left SIDE SEGMENT is UNATTESTED in the runtime (design §7.2 #2, side-segment placement) — carried at the design default and flagged for the maintainer sign-off packet. Rank values off the [V] group inverse axiom (genus:member:species:inverse, bridges.ttl:192) with family:group -> family:abelian:group, plus the :left side segment. Its term IRIs are in the abelian:group-scoped term: namespace so they never collide with the group inverse-left terms (EquationRecordShape identity-collision tooth)." .

# =====================================================================================
# (d7) EQUATION record — inverse-RIGHT (inherited, restated): inv(x)·x = e. rec:equation:record. [S] side seg
# =====================================================================================
alg:abelian:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:inverse:order:binary:family:abelian:group:genus:member:species:inverse:right:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record ;
    rdfs:label "abelian group inverse (right: inv(x)·x = e)" ;
    rel:notation "inv(x)·x = e" ;
    rel:left   term:inverse:right ;
    rel:right  term:inverse:e ;
    rel:member case:inverse:one ;
    rdfs:comment "[S] The RIGHT inverse law inv(x)·x = e — side 2 of the abelian-group two-sided inverse, INHERITED from group and restated at family:abelian:group, reified as an equation record (rec:equation:record) with one @rel:left term (inv(x)·x) and one @rel:right term (e). Its twin is the inverse-LEFT record above; together they are the TWO equation records the ONE two-sided inverse law decomposes into (design §1.6, §3). [S] the species:inverse:right SIDE SEGMENT is UNATTESTED (design §7.2 #2) — carried at the design default and flagged for the maintainer sign-off packet. Rank values off the [V] group inverse axiom (genus:member:species:inverse) with family:group -> family:abelian:group, plus the :right side segment. Distinct @rel:left term (term:inverse:right) from inverse-left (term:inverse:left), so the EquationRecordShape identity-collision sh:sparql does not fire between the twins; and abelian:group-scoped so no collision with the group inverse-right terms." .

# per-side reified case nodes for the inverse split (closure.ttl:185-192 case precedent).
case:inverse:zero rel:left term:inverse:left  ; rel:right term:inverse:e .
case:inverse:one  rel:left term:inverse:right ; rel:right term:inverse:e .

# =====================================================================================
# (d8) EQUATION record — COMMUTATIVITY, the SINGLE ADDED LAW: x·y = y·x. Dual-typed
#      rec:equation:record + rec:axiom:record (design §1.9 reuse side). ONE equation (single member),
#      not two-sided. Its OWN atom under subdomain/family abelian:group (Directive-17 no-cram, NOT
#      reusing the commutative-monoid commutativity atom). BYTE-IDENTICAL to bridges.ttl:180 (the
#      fnd:lawCommutativity closeMatch target). [D]
# =====================================================================================
alg:abelian:group:kingdom:axiom:phylum:operation:class:commutativity:order:binary:family:abelian:group:genus:composition:species:equality:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:equation:record , rec:axiom:record ;
    rdfs:label "abelian group commutativity" ;
    rel:notation "x·y = y·x" ;
    rel:left   term:comm:left ;
    rel:right  term:comm:right ;
    rel:member case:comm:zero ;
    rdfs:comment "[D] The COMMUTATIVITY law of the abelian-group theory — the SINGLE law abelian-group adds over group (one-law-per-child, algebra_spine.ttl:99-103,226) — as a reified equation record (rec:equation:record): the ordered pair x·y = y·x, one @rel:left term (x·y) and one @rel:right term (y·x) (the EquationRecordShape cardinality-1 tooth). It is minted as its OWN atom under subdomain abelian:group / family:abelian:group — DISTINCT from the commutative-monoid commutativity atom (spine/commutative_monoid.ttl:226, family:commutative:monoid): commutativity enters the tower at TWO independent spine points (over monoid -> commutative-monoid, and over group -> abelian-group), and Directive-17 no-cram mints a separate atom at each, never a single crammed shared atom. Dual-typed rec:axiom:record too (design §1.9: the runtime models each law as ONE kingdom:axiom…component:statement atom that is simultaneously the equation, avoiding the unattested component:equation — the §7.2 #7 reuse side, consistent with bridges.ttl:180 and records.ttl:76-81). Commutativity is a SINGLE equation (not two-sided): it does NOT decompose into member:left/member:right records the way the identity and inverse do (design §1.6). Rank values VERBATIM off the [V] group ASSOCIATIVITY axiom (genus:composition:species:equality — both are left=right equational laws over the binary product) with family:group -> family:abelian:group; this IRI is BYTE-IDENTICAL to bridges.ttl:180 (the fnd:lawCommutativity closeMatch target — the ONE fnd:lawCommutativity closeMatch-decomposes into this abelian:group atom AND the commutative:monoid commutativity atom, Directive-17 no-cram) so the merged alias map resolves. Its term IRIs live in the abelian:group-scoped term: namespace so they never collide with the commutative:monoid commutativity terms (EquationRecordShape identity-collision tooth). Its added-law status is teeth-proved by probes/abelian_group_law.rq (the commutativity probe) over the fixtures/ Z/3 witnesses (the non-commutative negative flips it RED, and — its single corrupted cell involving e — also flips the ModelShape identity tooth so the runner's fixture iteration catches it)." .

# per-side reified case node for commutativity (single member; closure.ttl:180-183 single-member idiom).
case:comm:zero rel:left term:comm:left ; rel:right term:comm:right .

# =====================================================================================
# (f) THEOREM + CERTIFICATE (design §2f — a theorem with a digest+proof-method certificate, NEVER an
#     axiom; the closure.ttl Yoneda theorem/certificate idiom, :129-142). The natural STRUCTURE theorem
#     of an abelian group: the inverse of a product is the product of the inverses WITHOUT reversal.
# =====================================================================================
alg:abelian:group:kingdom:theorem:phylum:algebra:class:inverse:order:declarative:family:abelian:group:genus:product:species:inverse:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , rec:theorem:record ;
    rdfs:label "abelian group inverse-of-product" ;
    rel:notation "(x·y)^-1 = x^-1·y^-1 (no order reversal)" ;
    rel:certificate alg:abelian:group:kingdom:certificate:phylum:algebra:class:inverse:order:declarative:family:abelian:group:genus:product:species:inverse:component:statement:instance:canonical ;
    rel:authority "SYN" ;
    rel:created  "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:modified "2026-09-06T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    rel:version  "1"^^xsd:nonNegativeInteger ;
    rel:state    "accepted" ;
    rdfs:comment "The natural STRUCTURE theorem of an abelian group — the inverse of a product is the product of the inverses WITHOUT order reversal, a theorem NOT an additional foundational axiom (design §2f, the closure.ttl Yoneda theorem/certificate idiom, :129-142): in any abelian group (S,·,e) the inverse of a product equals the product of the inverses, (x·y)^-1 = x^-1·y^-1 for all x,y — WHEREAS in a general (possibly non-commutative) group only the reversed law (x·y)^-1 = y^-1·x^-1 holds. It is a DERIVED CONSEQUENCE of the single commutativity axiom together with the group axioms and the group inverse-uniqueness theorem (spine/group.ttl): (x·y)·(x^-1·y^-1) = x·(y·x^-1)·y^-1 = x·(x^-1·y)·y^-1 (commutativity swaps y·x^-1 = x^-1·y) = (x·x^-1)·(y·y^-1) = e·e = e, and symmetrically (x^-1·y^-1)·(x·y) = e, so x^-1·y^-1 is the two-sided inverse of x·y and by inverse uniqueness (x·y)^-1 = x^-1·y^-1 — the D24 A0 ProofArtifact plane, not a new axiom, and precisely WHY commutativity is the abelian-group's characteristic addition (it collapses the reversal). It is a rec:theorem:record carrying a @rel:certificate (a proof artifact with a digest + proof-method), NEVER a rec:axiom:record — the theorem/axiom collapse is forbidden (rec:axiom:record owl:disjointWith rec:theorem:record, records.ttl:119; design §2f). Provenance quartet + @rel:authority 'SYN' on the record (synthesized cited-standard-math; it derives from the SYN commutativity and inverse laws). [S] kingdom:theorem class:inverse / genus:product / species:inverse are UNATTESTED (§7.2 #1) -> sign-off packet." .

alg:abelian:group:kingdom:certificate:phylum:algebra:class:inverse:order:declarative:family:abelian:group:genus:product:species:inverse:component:statement:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , typ:certificate ;
    rdfs:label "abelian group inverse-of-product certificate" ;
    rel:digest:value    "6a361e7b4e93065c9a4872a40bc2c19164101c0bd627f6d8e2cd05fb52512de0" ;
    rel:proof:method    "Explicit general mathematical derivation ((x.y).(x^-1.y^-1) = (x.x^-1).(y.y^-1) = e via commutativity, symmetrically on the other side, then inverse uniqueness); not proof-assistant checked" ;
    rel:source:location "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-06-w2-sp0-primordial-fold-design.md#2f" ;
    rdfs:comment "The proof CERTIFICATE for abelian-group inverse-of-product (design §2f; the closure.ttl certificate idiom, :132/137/142): a proof artifact carrying @rel:digest:value (the SHA-256 of the canonical proof statement 'Abelian group inverse-of-product: in any abelian group (S,.,e) the inverse of a product equals the product of the inverses without reversal, (x.y)^-1 = x^-1.y^-1 for all x,y. Proof: (x.y).(x^-1.y^-1) = x.(y.x^-1).y^-1 = x.(x^-1.y).y^-1 = (x.x^-1).(y.y^-1) = e.e = e, using commutativity to swap y.x^-1 = x^-1.y, and symmetrically (x^-1.y^-1).(x.y) = e; so x^-1.y^-1 is the two-sided inverse of x.y, and by inverse uniqueness (x.y)^-1 = x^-1.y^-1. General mathematical derivation; not proof-assistant checked.'), @rel:proof:method (an explicit general derivation, honestly NOT a proof-assistant certificate — D20 honesty) and @rel:source:location. It is typed @typ:certificate, NEVER an axiom — an axiom is asserted, a certificate records a derivation. This is the ProofArtifact plane made concrete: the theorem points at it via @rel:certificate, so a theorem stripped of its certificate is detectable, and an axiom masquerading as a proved theorem is caught by the axiom/theorem disjointness (records.ttl:119). The digest is reproducible: sha256 of the quoted canonical statement equals the recorded value." .

# =====================================================================================
# (g) GATE — the Plane-3 reconciliation gate of the triad envelope (design §2g, @typ:gate).
# =====================================================================================
alg:abelian:group:kingdom:assignment:phylum:reconciliation:class:gate:order:declarative:family:abelian:group:genus:reconciled:species:declaration:component:assignment:instance:canonical
    a owl:NamedIndividual , typ:gate ;
    rdfs:label "abelian group declaration reconciliation gate" ;
    rel:check:status   "declaration reconciled; not a generic semantic proof" ;
    rel:interpreted:by alg:abelian:group:kingdom:interpretation:phylum:reconciliation:class:declaration:order:declarative:family:abelian:group:genus:reconciled:species:abelian:group:component:interpretation:instance:canonical ;
    rdfs:comment "The Plane-3 reconciliation GATE of the declaration triad envelope (design §2g): the theory record (@typ:declaration) @rel:assignment-points at this gate, which records that the abelian-group declaration was RECONCILED against its denotatum — @rel:check:status 'declaration reconciled; not a generic semantic proof' (the honest scope: the gate reconciles the declaration to the denoted object, it does not claim a universal semantic proof) — and @rel:interpreted:by an interpretation atom. Typed @typ:gate. This is the per-record triad-envelope gate INSTANCE (Plane-3), NOT a gate SPECIFICATION class (the two-ladder ruling, design §4 / §7.2 #8: gate/clause SPECS mint the core:entity gate ladder; this per-record gate instance rides the mathematics ladder scoped to the abelian-group rung, adjective-first B1). It closes the Denotatum/DeclarationRecord/Gate triad (D24 four planes) so the abelian-group declaration is reconciled, not merely asserted." .

